The flow is built and ready. Here's a summary of what was created:

**File:** `ExpenseApproval/ExpenseApproval/ExpenseApproval.flow`

### What was built

| Node | Type | Role |
|---|---|---|
| Manual Trigger | `core.trigger.manual` | Entry point |
| Prepare Expense | `core.action.script` | Validates name, description, amount; throws on bad input; builds a human-readable summary |
| Manager Review | `uipath.human-in-the-loop.quick-form` | Sends a task to **expense-approvers** group via Action Center + Email; shows employee name, description, amount, receipt URL, summary; manager picks **Approve** or **Reject** and optionally adds comments |
| Manager Decision | `core.logic.decision` | Routes on `status === "Approve"` |
| Log Approved / Log Rejected / Log Error | `core.action.script` | Returns `approvalStatus` + `managerComments` for each path |
| Done ×3 | `core.control.end` | Maps `approvalStatus` and `managerComments` as flow outputs on every terminal path |

**Flow inputs:** `employeeName`, `expenseDescription`, `amount`, `receiptUrl`
**Flow outputs:** `approvalStatus` (`"Approved"` / `"Rejected"` / `"Error"`), `managerComments`

The `prepareExpense` error port is wired — if required fields are missing or `amount ≤ 0`, the flow routes to the error path instead of faulting the whole instance.

